  "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=3+\\text{i}.$*",
